<title>USA: Case stock jumps on stock buyback.</title>
<headline>Case stock jumps on stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>RACINE, Wis.</dateline>
<text>
<p>The stock of Case Corp., an agricultural and constructiuon equipment maker, jumped Wednesday after the company said it would repurchase up to 4 million shares of its stock.</p>
<p>Case was up $4 at $61.50 on the New York Stock Exchange in afternoon trading. The 4 million shares represent 5 percent of Case's 74 million common shares.</p>
<p>Timing of the programme will be determined by financial and market conditions, the company said. The stock has benefited over the past two days from a strong industry forecast Tuesday by its close competitor Deere &amp; Co.</p>
</text>
